  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a hybrid quantum–classical LSTM for fraud detection using a 10‑qubit variational quantum circuit simulated with PennyLane. On a 10k‑sample balanced dataset it achieves 95.33% accuracy, 96.67% recall, and 95.39% F1, slightly outperforming a classical LSTM baseline (94.33% accuracy) but with much higher training cost (~55 s vs ~1.5 s per epoch). Scaling experiments with larger datasets and up to 12 qubits reach ~98% accuracy but remain simulator-based.",
